# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for builds with
# IMPRESARIO_SANITIZERS=undefined. See docs/sanitizers.md.
#
# Qt's slot objects and message handler are called through function pointers of
# a different type, which -fsanitize=function reports; this is how Qt works.
# The vptr entries are type checks on objects whose type information comes from
# another shared library (Qt D-Bus, Boost), which the check cannot match.
function:QtPrivate::QSlotObjectBase::call
function:QtPrivate::QSlotObjectBase::destroyIfLastRef
function:qt_message_print
vptr:QDBusConnection::~QDBusConnection
vptr:boost::detail::shared_count::~shared_count
vptr:boost::detail::sp_counted_base::release
vptr:boost::detail::sp_counted_base::weak_release
